# A top-level `let` whose value is a widget named as a blueprint value, built by a widget
# of the module (Semantics ch. 3: `let` for values; ch. 8: a blueprint is an opaque handle
# and still a value, built where a block applies it). `ValuedWidgets` reads no top-level
# `let`'s value. Reaches `WidgetNamed`'s refusal "the widget function @One as a value"
# on prismc-r27.
# Written by Claude (t2, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@One: @unit
@One:
    Ui.Label($text=$"one")

let @shown = @One

@page: @unit
@page:
    @shown                                                             # 0
